    {
      "text": "convicted by their own conscience, John 8:9. pricked in their heart, Acts 2:37. lived in all good conscience before God, Acts 23:1. conscience void of offence toward God, Acts 24:16. their conscience also bearing witness, Rom. 2:15 (9:1–2). ye must needs be subject … for conscience sake, Rom. 13:5. their conscience being weak is defiled, 1 Cor. 8:7. why is my liberty judged of another man’s conscience, 1 Cor. 10:29. commending ourselves to every man’s conscience, 2 Cor. 4:2. we … are made manifest in your consciences, 2 Cor. 5:11. being past feeling have given themselves over unto lasciviousness, Eph. 4:19. charity out of a pure heart, and of a good conscience, 1 Tim. 1:5. Holding the mystery of the faith in a pure conscience, 1 Tim. 3:9. having their conscience seared with a hot iron, 1 Tim. 4:2. I serve from my forefathers with pure conscience, 2 Tim. 1:3. even their mind and conscience is defiled, Titus 1:15. purge your conscience from dead works, Heb. 9:14. hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience, Heb. 10:22. we have a good conscience, in all things, Heb. 13:18. if a man for conscience toward God endure grief, 1 Pet. 2:19. Having a good conscience, 1 Pet. 3:16.",
